# Every lifecycle event sent through POST /trades/trigger-event, the event named as a parameter. As in the other API
# snippets the request is built in one step and sent in the next. The request is the case's own row
# (data/api/<event>.json, chosen by the case ID) with its tradeIds replaced by the stored trade; the event name and the
# word before "data" (valid, malformed, duplicate) are for the reader, the row is what is sent. The outcomes compare the
# response with the case's recording. A new event needs no snippet here: case data, recordings and the feature. Evidence
# beyond the response (notional reduced, trade closed) stays in the event's own api/<feature>.snippet.

# ── Build request ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

@When "^(maker|checker) has (?:valid|malformed|duplicate) data for the '([^']*)' event$"
    Given build json request from current scenario with trade id from stored variable 'createdTradeId' as user '$1'

# ── Make api call ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

@When "^performs the '([^']*)' event via api$"
    When post to path '/trades/trigger-event'
    And attach the response body to the report

# ── Assertions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@Then "^the '([^']*)' event is executed successfully$"
    Then the '$1' should be 'executed' successfully

@Then "^the '([^']*)' event is rejected with a validation error$"
    Then failed to 'execute' '$1'

@Then "^the '([^']*)' event is rejected with a business rule violation$"
    Then failed to 'execute' '$1'
